# Scoped to perception/ so the repo root's .gitignore is untouched.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Recordings. Large binaries; they are inputs, not source.
assets/recordings/
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.avi

# Live captures from tools/record_match.py. A 4-minute match at 10 fps is
# ~2,400 lossless PNGs, ~1.5 GB -- same reasoning as assets/recordings/, but
# the rule has to exist BEFORE the first recording, not after.
assets/live/

# Templates cropped from a specific recording at a specific resolution --
# regenerable from the recording, and meaningless without it.
#
# Written as `config/templates/*` rather than `config/templates/` so the
# exception below can work at all: git does not descend into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so a negation for a path inside one is never even evaluated.
config/templates/*

# ...except the tower-HP digits, which are committed. Two reasons the rule
# above does not hold for them:
#
#   "Regenerable from the recording" is not true on a fresh clone, because
#   assets/recordings/ is itself ignored a few lines up. Nobody but this
#   machine can rebuild them.
#
#   tests/test_tower_numerals.py asserts an end-to-end reading against them.
#   Without the files that test SKIPS rather than fails, which is the kind of
#   silent hole the rest of this package is written to avoid.
#
# 4.6 KB for the set. Rebuild with tools/build_tower_digit_templates.py.
!config/templates/tower_549x976/

# Generated reports.
out/
*.divergence.json

# Replay fixtures ARE committed (tests/assets/*.json) -- they are small and
# the tests depend on them. Not ignored here on purpose: python_ai/replays/ is
# rewritten continuously by the training run, so a test bound to it passes or
# fails depending on when it runs.

# Extra virtualenvs created for the ClashRoyaleBuildABot evaluation. The
# existing ".venv/" rule does not match these -- it matches only that exact
# name -- and they are ~2GB together.
.venv-*/

# ADB, downloaded on demand by clashroyalebuildabot/emulator/emulator.py from
# Google's official platform-tools URL. ~25MB of redistributable binaries that
# regenerate themselves on first run; no reason to carry them in git.
clashroyalebuildabot/emulator/platform-tools/
clashroyalebuildabot/emulator/*.zip
